<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed weaker at 1.19 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed weaker at 1.19 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.4890 to the dollar, down from 3.4710 on Monday and at 1.9015 to the mark, up from 1.9065, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of minus 1.19 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, weaker than Monday's minus 1.07 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
